# QA Agent — Goal flow (authoritative)

The Mermaid sequence below is the **implementation goal**. Behavior must match it end-to-end.

**Mapping:** `Claude CLI` in the diagram = the dedicated **Claude CLI GitHub Action** (inner job step). Its input and output are Action I/O and must be saved as **artifacts**. `QA Agent` = the QA Agent Action / our orchestration in `src/qa-agent/`. Do not spawn Claude from Node.

There is a **single flow** (no plan-only / plan-and-run modes): generate → validate → run all cases → comment → fail if any case failed.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant Dev as Developer
  participant GH as GitHub
  participant GHA as GitHub Action
  participant Agent as QA Agent
  participant Claude as Claude CLI
  participant PW as Playwright
  participant HTTP as HTTP checks

  Dev->>GH: Creates or updates a pull request
  GH->>GHA: Starts the workflow for this PR
  GHA->>GHA: Checks out the repo and installs Claude CLI
  GHA->>Agent: Starts the agent with its settings

  Agent->>GH: Reads the PR diff, changed files, and description
  GH-->>Agent: Returns the PR context

  Note over Agent,Claude: Claude runs in readonly mode for planning
  Agent->>Claude: Ask to generate new test cases as JSON matching our JSON Schema
  Note over Claude: Here new test cases are generated
  Claude-->>Agent: Returns generated test cases as JSON

  Agent->>Agent: Checks that the JSON matches the schema

  alt The JSON does not match the schema
    Agent->>Claude: Send the validation errors and ask to fix the JSON
    Claude-->>Agent: Returns fixed test cases JSON
    Agent->>Agent: Checks the JSON against the schema again
  end

  Note over Agent: From here we use the generated test cases

  loop For each test case
    alt The case is a UI test
      Agent->>PW: Open the page and run the steps
      PW-->>Agent: Returns pass or fail plus a screenshot
    else The case is an API HTTP check
      Agent->>HTTP: Send the HTTP request and check the response
      HTTP-->>Agent: Returns pass or fail
    end
  end
  Agent->>GHA: Save screenshots and logs as artifacts
  Agent->>GH: Posts the test cases and run results as a PR comment
  alt Any case failed
    Agent-->>GHA: Mark the job as failed
  else All cases passed
    Agent-->>GHA: Mark the job as success
  end

  GHA-->>GH: Publishes the check status on the PR
  GH-->>Dev: Shows the comment and pass or fail status
```

When rules conflict with informal notes, **this diagram wins** for control flow. Claude-as-dedicated-Action + artifact I/O still apply as the how for the Agent↔Claude arrows.
